 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "adverbes d'intensité et de manière : très, assez, vraiment, vite, bien, -ment",
   "en": "adverbs of degree and manner: très, assez, vraiment, vite, bien, -ment"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "très, assez, vraiment, trop는 형용사나 부사 앞에서 정도를 나타냅니다. 방법 부사는 동사를 꾸미며 보통 여성형 형용사 + -ment로 만듭니다 (lent → lentement, prudent → prudemment). vite, dur처럼 형태가 같은 부사도 있고, bon의 부사는 bien입니다.",
   "en": "Très, assez, vraiment and trop go before an adjective or adverb to show degree. Manner adverbs describe a verb and are usually feminine adjective + -ment (lent → lentement, prudent → prudemment). Some adverbs keep the same form (vite, dur) and the adverb of bon is bien."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Structure",
    "예 / Exemple"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "très / assez / vraiment",
     "Ce film était très intéressant."
    ],
    [
     "trop + adj.",
     "Le café est trop chaud."
    ],
    [
     "형용사 + -ment",
     "Conduisez prudemment. Parlez lentement."
    ],
    [
     "vite / bien",
     "Il court vite. Elle parle bien anglais."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "정도 부사는 형용사 앞.",
    "en": "Degree adverbs go before the adjective."
   },
   {
    "ko": "-ant → -amment, -ent → -emment.",
    "en": "-ant → -amment, -ent → -emment."
   },
   {
    "ko": "bon → bien.",
    "en": "bon → bien."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
